{"stage":"design","what":"arm B -- the five leaking stems rewritten to withhold the premise the key asserts; every option, key, explanation and other field byte-identical, verified mechanically before running","control":"all 15 option permutations identical to arm A, so position is controlled and the STEM is the only difference","stem_rewrites_by":"quiz-generator (sonnet). The orchestrator writes no question text.","ok":true}
{"stage":"RESULT","arm_A":"15/15 (100%)","arm_B":"14/15 (93%)","verdict":"THE STEM HYPOTHESIS FAILED. Withholding the premises did essentially nothing -- one hit lost out of fifteen.","ok":true}
{"stage":"flaw-in-my-own-test","what":"w02 was not a clean test and I should have caught it before spawning -- its distractor B still reads 'Since both performers scored an identical 1.0', so the fact removed from the stem survived in an option","mitigation":"the other four were rewritten cleanly and three still scored 3/3, so the conclusion does not rest on w02","sub-lesson":"a premise cannot be withheld by editing the stem alone","ok":false}
{"stage":"options-only-probe","spawns":6,"design":"four options, NO stem at all, 'which is the intended correct answer?'","result":"4/6 (67%) against 25% chance","ladder":{"whole_question":"100%","stem_premises_withheld":"93%","no_stem_at_all":"67%","chance":"25%"},"reading":"deleting the question costs about a third of the excess over chance; the OPTION SET keeps most of it","suspect":"distractor plausibility -- the wrong answers are recognisably wrong to someone who knows nothing, so the reader picks the survivor","consistent_with":"runs/tier4-control's own finding on its one leaking fabricated item","ok":true}
{"stage":"why-the-rubric-misses-it","observation":"nearly every ENFORCED distractor rule is about surface -- relative length, hedge density, absolute quantifiers, grammatical type. The rule that would catch an unbelievable distractor is D3 (no straw distractor), which is a critic judgement, and the P2 stability run found the critic applying its reasons inconsistently.","examples":["a question asking which objection has the most support carries an option saying there is no objection to raise","a question asking what is wrong with an explanation carries an option saying nothing is wrong"],"ok":true}
{"stage":"limits","items":["n=6 on the options-only probe; the 67% could move a lot","w08 scored 0/3 WITH its stem and was answered correctly from options alone -- at this sample size individual items are noise","'the leak is in the distractors' rests on one failed hypothesis and one 6-trial probe. It is a lead, not a conclusion.","the next test is the same shape and just as cheap: rewrite the DISTRACTORS, hold stem and key fixed, re-measure"]}
